evidence\sprints\sprint-3\2026-09-15-planning.md:245:Sprint 3 close-out will consolidate implementation status, user feedback, performanc…20028 tokens truncated…ten requirements;\r\n- demonstrate consistent use of the agreed project methodology;\r\n- maintain traceability between requirements, issues, branches, commits and Pull Requests;\r\n- provide evidence of planning for the Sprint 1 milestone.\r\n\r\nThe backlog is a planning tool and must remain current as requirements, stakeholder feedback and technical decisions develop.\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\r\n### Included\r\n\r\n- Review all current Gitea issues.\r\n- Identify which existing issues already cover project requirements.\r\n- Map existing issues to the relevant project requirements.\r\n- Avoid creating duplicate issues.\r\n- Create missing issues for the complete project lifecycle.\r\n- Include project-wide, Basic, Intermediate and Advanced requirements.\r\n- Create separate issues for meaningful units of work.\r\n- Assign the correct issue template to each issue.\r\n- Add applicable type, area, tier and priority labels.\r\n- Assign each issue to the appropriate milestone.\r\n- Place newly created issues in the Backlog board column.\r\n- Identify dependencies between major issues.\r\n- Identify blockers and high-risk work.\r\n- Prioritise urgent Sprint 1 foundation and vertical-slice work.\r\n- Record stakeholder questions where a requirement needs clarification.\r\n- Create or update a repository backlog and requirements-traceability document.\r\n- Review the initial backlog with the team.\r\n- Update the backlog after relevant stakeholder feedback.\r\n\r\n### Excluded\r\n\r\n- Implementing the features represented by the backlog issues.\r\n- Completing all Basic, Intermediate or Advanced functionality.\r\n- Assigning every future issue to a team member before it is ready.\r\n- Moving every issue into Sprint 1.\r\n- Creating duplicate issues for work already represented in Gitea.\r\n- Fully refining every distant Sprint 2 and Sprint 3 issue before its requirements are sufficiently understood.\r\n- Treating the initial backlog as permanently fixed.\r\n\r\n## Backlog Structure\r\n\r\nEach issue must contain, at minimum:\r\n\r\n- a clear title;\r\n- an appropriate issue template;\r\n- applicable labels;\r\n- an appropriate milestone;\r\n- an initial board position.\r\n\r\nIssues being prepared for immediate implementation must also contain:\r\n\r\n- a clear description;\r\n- motivation;\r\n- included and excluded scope;\r\n- acceptance criteria;\r\n- dependencies;\r\n- testing or verification requirements;\r\n- documentation and evidence requirements;\r\n- an assignee;\r\n- a suggested branch name.\r\n\r\nLater-sprint issues may initially contain a concise scope summary. They must be fully refined before being moved from `Backlog` to `Ready`.\r\n\r\n## Prioritisation Order\r\n\r\nThe backlog must be prioritised in the following order:\r\n\r\n1. Project blockers and unresolved stakeholder decisions.\r\n2. Sprint 1 setup and methodology evidence.\r\n3. The event-driven Basic vertical slice.\r\n4. Remaining Basic requirements.\r\n5. Intermediate batch, review, aggregation, performance and API-consumer requirements.\r\n6. Advanced statistic-definition, live-feed, temporal and reconciliation requirements.\r\n7. Final hardening, documentation, demonstration and submission work.\r\n\r\nSecurity, testing, documentation and accessibility must be included throughout the project rather than left entirely until the final milestone.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance Criteria\r\n\r\n- [ ] All existing Gitea issues have been reviewed before new issues are created.\r\n- [ ] Existing issues covering catalogue work have been mapped rather than recreated.\r\n- [ ] Duplicate or substantially overlapping issues have been removed, combined or clearly distinguished.\r\n- [ ] All requirements applying to every COMS3011A project are represented in the backlog.\r\n- [ ] All Sport Analytics Basic requirements are represented in the backlog.\r\n- [ ] All Sport Analytics Intermediate requirements are represented in the backlog.\r\n- [ ] All Sport Analytics Advanced requirements are represented in the backlog.\r\n- [ ] Testing, documentation, accessibility, security, deployment and stakeholder-interaction work are represented.\r\n- [ ] Final submission, reporting and presentation work are represented.\r\n- [ ] Every issue has an appropriate title, template, labels and milestone.\r\n- [ ] Newly created issues initially appear in the Backlog board column.\r\n- [ ] Urgent Sprint 1 issues have complete descriptions and acceptance criteria before implementation begins.\r\n- [ ] Later issues have enough information to identify their purpose and requirement coverage.\r\n- [ ] High-priority and high-risk issues are clearly labelled.\r\n- [ ] Major dependencies and blockers are recorded.\r\n- [ ] The backlog supports a Basic vertical slice during Sprint 1.\r\n- [ ] The backlog targets Basic and Intermediate completion before Advanced work is considered complete.\r\n- [ ] Advanced architectural risks are scheduled early enough that they are not all deferred until Sprint 3.\r\n- [ ] A backlog or requirements-traceability document is added to the repository or documentation site.\r\n- [ ] The backlog has been reviewed by the group.\r\n- [ ] Relevant stakeholder questions are recorded for the next stakeholder meeting.\r\n- [ ] Changes resulting from stakeholder feedback are reflected in the relevant issues.\r\n- [ ] The work is reviewed and merged through a Pull Request where repository documentation is changed.\r\n\r\n## Suggested Repository Deliverable\r\n\r\nCreate or update:\r\n\r\n```text\r\ndocs/planning/project-backlog.md\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe document should contain:\r\n\r\n- the issue number;\r\n- issue title;\r\n- requirement tier;\r\n- milestone;\r\n- priority;\r\n- current status;\r\n- dependencies;\r\n- the requirement or rubric criterion covered.\r\n\r\nThis document must reference Gitea as the authoritative live work tracker. It should not become a second independent backlog that is allowed to contradict Gitea.\r\n\r\n## Dependencies\r\n\r\nThis issue depends on access to:\r\n\r\n- the COMS3011A Project Brief;\r\n- the Sport Analytics project-specific brief;\r\n- the COMS3011A AI Policy;\r\n- the approved Project Methodology;\r\n- the approved Git Methodology;\r\n- the existing Gitea issue list;\r\n- the Gitea Project board and milestones.\r\n\r\nThere are no implementation dependencies.\r\n\r\n## Testing and Verification\r\n\r\nThe backlog must be verified by:\r\n\r\n1. Comparing all created or mapped issues against the project-wide requirements.\r\n2. Comparing all created or mapped issues against the Sport Analytics Basic requirements.\r\n3. Comparing all created or mapped issues against the Sport Analytics Intermediate requirements.\r\n4. Comparing all created or mapped issues against the Sport Analytics Advanced requirements.\r\n5. Checking that no requirement is represented only by an untracked conversation or informal note.\r\n6. Checking that issues can be filtered by milestone, type, area and requirement tier.\r\n7. Checking that urgent Sprint 1 issues have sufficient acceptance criteria to move to `Ready`.\r\n8. Checking that existing completed work points to its original issue rather than a duplicate retrospective issue.\r\n\r\n## Documentation and Evidence\r\n\r\nEvidence for this issue must include:\r\n\r\n- links to the created and mapped Gitea issues;\r\n- the populated Gitea Project board;\r\n- the completed backlog or requirements-traceability document;\r\n- labels and milestones visible on the issues;\r\n- a record of the team backlog review;\r\n- stakeholder questions or decisions arising from backlog refinement;\r\n- the linked Pull Request for any repository documentation changes.\r\n\r\n## Definition of Done\r\n\r\nThis issue is complete when:\r\n\r\n- the complete initial project backlog exists;\r\n- existing issues have been mapped;\r\n- missing issues have been created;\r\n- all major project requirements are traceable to issues;\r\n- the urgent Sprint 1 backlog is fully refined;\r\n- later work is assigned to an appropriate milestone;\r\n- the group has reviewed the backlog;\r\n- the repository backlog or traceability document has been merged;\r\n- the Gitea board accurately reflects the agreed priorities.\r\n\r\nCompleting this issue does not mean that the individual backlog issues have been implemented.\r\n\r\n## Git and Pull Request Requirements\r\n\r\nAfter the issue number is assigned:\r\n\r\n1. Create a branch using:\r\n\r\n   ```text\r\n   docs/\u003cissue-number\u003e-project-backlog\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n2. Use a commit such as:\r\n\r\n   ```text\r\n   docs(project): add complete project backlog plan\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n3. Reference the issue in the commit body:\r\n\r\n   ```text\r\n   Refs #\u003cissue-number\u003e\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n4. Open a Pull Request linked to this issue.\r\n\r\n5. Include the following in the Pull Request:\r\n\r\n   - purpose;\r\n   - backlog summary;\r\n   - requirement coverage;\r\n   - verification performed;\r\n   - known gaps or stakeholder questions;\r\n   - documentation changes.\r\n\r\n6. Close the issue through the Pull Request using:\r\n\r\n   ```text\r\n   Closes #\u003cissue-number\u003e\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n## AI Declaration\r\n\r\n\u003e The preceding issue was planned and generated with the assistance of ChatGPT-Web[GPT-5.6 Thinking].","ref":"","assets":[],"labels":[{"id":9,"name":"area: documentation","exclusive":false,"is_archived":false,"color":"bfe5bf","description":"","url":"https://sdp.ms.wits.ac.za/api/v1/repos/git-push-pray/Sport-Analytics-Tool/labels/9"},{"id":37,"name":"priority: high","exclusive":false,"is_archived":false,"color":"f6c6c7","description":"","url":"https://sdp.ms.wits.ac.za/api/v1/repos/git-push-pray/Sport-Analytics-Tool/labels/37"},{"id":44,"name":"tier: common","exclusive":false,"is_archived":false,"color":"d4c5f9